The positions and sizes FILE_POSITION, FILE_SIZE and FILE_SEEK use depend
on the file's format, which IEEE 1076-2019 leaves to the implementation.
xezim writes GHDL's binary format (a header, then each INTEGER in 4 bytes);
nvc writes 8 bytes per INTEGER without a header, so its numbers differ.
The golden is IEEE 1076-2019 §5.5.2 applied to xezim's format: the file
holds 10, 20, 30, 40, 50 in 20 bytes (the header not counted); byte 8 is
the third element, 4 bytes after position 12 the fifth, and the last 4
bytes the fifth.
